.TH HAMSTIK 1 "HAMSTIK RELEASE EDIT"
.SH NAME
hamstik release edit \- Edit a release version
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hamstik release edit [OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Edit a release version
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I ID
Release version id (UUID)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --name
New name
.TP
.B --display-version
New display version label
.TP
.B --clear-display-version
Clear the display version label
Choices: true, false
.TP
.B --description
New description text
.TP
.B --description-file
New description source (path, or - for stdin)
.TP
.B --description-editor
Author the description in $VISUAL/$EDITOR instead of passing text
Choices: true, false
.TP
.B --clear-description
Clear the description
Choices: true, false
.TP
.B --owner
New release owner: me, a user UUID, a public ID (usr_...), or `none`
.TP
.B --target-date
New target date
.TP
.B --clear-target-date
Clear the target date
Choices: true, false
.TP
.B --release-date
New release date
.TP
.B --clear-release-date
Clear the release date
Choices: true, false
.TP
.B --force
Bypass revision conflict protection (If-Match: *)
Choices: true, false
.TP
.B --project
Project key (overrides context)
.TP
.B --idempotency-key
Explicit idempotency key
